From 8c6f9e94e66a167a2a897c45f7351fde64320701 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:36:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the location-search hint text unselectable

A click-drag or triple-click on the "District name in English or
Arabic..." hint under the Location filter left it visibly highlighted
in blue in screenshots, reading as an unintended style. It was always
just the browser's normal text-selection highlight, but disabling
selection on that line means it can never appear that way again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016tuWiGwhPRZEv1TzRpDFYk
---
 templates/properties/index.html | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/templates/properties/index.html b/templates/properties/index.html
index 8aa785d..a5020ea 100644
--- a/templates/properties/index.html
+++ b/templates/properties/index.html
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
       <div class="field">
         <label>{{ t('Location') }}</label>
         <input type="text" name="area" value="{{ f.area }}" placeholder="{{ t('e.g. The Pearl, مشيرب, or zone 51') }}">
-        <div class="small" style="color:var(--faint);margin-top:4px">{{ t('District name in English or Arabic, a close spelling, or a zone number all work.') }}</div>
+        <div class="small" style="color:var(--faint);margin-top:4px;user-select:none">{{ t('District name in English or Arabic, a close spelling, or a zone number all work.') }}</div>
       </div>
       <div class="field">
         <label>{{ t('Type') }}</label>
-- 
2.43.0

